              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner (Eric H. Zagrans), according to Petitioner (Eric H. Zagrans), the petitioner argues that Merrell\u202fDow\u2019s holding that federal statutory violations are not substantial enough to confer jurisdiction unless Congress created a private right of action should be applied here."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "2399200d0077b50f321266882146f797b6767821b54ebd2b4d279b166240801f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-2399200d0077-0000-0004"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 7,
                "start": 7
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The petitioner contends that the focus should be on the federal interest, not the state interest, when determining congressional intent for federal\u2011question jurisdiction."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Zagrans",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "2399200d0077b50f321266882146f797b6767821b54ebd2b4d279b166240801f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-2399200d0077-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 19,
                "start": 19
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Zagrans, the petitioner emphasizes that the test for a substantial federal question hinges on whether the federal issue is essential to the state cause of action."
        }
